{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf.cljc | sed -n '205,240p;268,285p;344,365p;382,395p'\"","aggregated_output":"   205\t   UCF mints no second addressing scheme.\"\n   206\t  [v]\n   207\t  (jing/segment-key v))\n   208\t\n   209\t\n   210\t(defn canonicalize\n   211\t  \"Code identity as one S7.9 outcome. On success\n   212\t   `{:yin.k/status :yin.k/ok, :yin.code/vector v, :yin.code/hash address,\n   213\t   :yin.k/contract contract-stamp}`; otherwise the `refusal` map the\n   214\t   vector function would have thrown.\n   215\t\n   216\t   `contract` is the batch's own semantic stamp, required and compared\n   217\t   with `vm/semantic-contract` first (`:contract-missing`,\n   218\t   `:contract-mismatch`, thrown): the outcome's stamp is the one verified,\n   219\t   never one assigned on the caller's behalf, so canonicalizing cannot\n   220\t   relabel an old or unstamped batch.\"\n   221\t  [datoms contract]\n   222\t  (vm/check-contract! vm/semantic-contract contract)\n   223\t  (try\n   224\t    (let [v (batch->canonical-instruction-vector datoms)]\n   225\t      {:yin.k/status :yin.k/ok,\n   226\t       :yin.code/vector v,\n   227\t       :yin.code/hash (code-address v),\n   228\t       :yin.k/contract contract-stamp})\n   229\t    (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) e\n   230\t      (let [data (ex-data e)]\n   231\t        (if (= :yin.k/non-portable (:yin.k/status data))\n   232\t          data\n   233\t          (throw e))))))\n   234\t\n   235\t\n   236\t;; =============================================================================\n   237\t;; Safepoints (S7.4)\n   238\t;; =============================================================================\n   239\t\n   240\t(def transitions\n   268\t   :stream-put :parking,\n   269\t   :ffi-call :parking,\n   270\t   :call :parking})\n   271\t\n   272\t\n   273\t(def ^:private parking-reasons\n   274\t  \"S7.4.1's safepoint kinds, by parking mnemonic. An `:ffi-call` parks\n   275\t   under two reasons -- sent, or retained while the request is in hand --\n   276\t   at one safepoint.\"\n   277\t  {:park [:park],\n   278\t   :stream-next [:next],\n   279\t   :stream-put [:put],\n   280\t   :ffi-call [:ffi :ffi-request],\n   281\t   :call [:call-effect]})\n   282\t\n   283\t\n   284\t(defn stack-effect\n   285\t  \"Delta |St| across one parking instruction, from the tuple alone\n   344\t  \"The static safepoint map of one canonical vector (S7.4.2): one entry per\n   345\t   parking instruction, each carrying only what the vector alone fixes --\n   346\t   the parking pc, the canonical resume pc (pc+1, always inside the segment\n   347\t   by S2.6), the reasons under which the machine parks there, the stack\n   348\t   effect across the instruction, and the lexically required names at the\n   349\t   resume pc. Absolute depth, activation bases, captured environments and\n   350\t   physical layouts are not here: they ride in the frame\n   351\t   (`activation-state`).\"\n   352\t  [v]\n   353\t  (into []\n   354\t        (keep-indexed\n   355\t          (fn [pc t]\n   356\t            (when (= :parking (get transitions (nth t 0)))\n   357\t              {:yin.safepoint/at pc,\n   358\t               :yin.safepoint/pc (inc pc),\n   359\t               :yin.safepoint/reasons (get parking-reasons (nth t 0)),\n   360\t               :yin.safepoint/stack-effect (stack-effect t),\n   361\t               :yin.safepoint/lexically-required\n   362\t               (lexically-required v (inc pc))})))\n   363\t        v))\n   364\t\n   365\t\n   382\t\n   383\t\n   384\t(defn activation-state\n   385\t  \"The dynamic half of a parked configuration, read off a frame -- a wait\n   386\t   entry or parked record `{segment pc env stack k}` -- never derived from\n   387\t   code: the absolute operand-stack depth, the names E actually binds, and\n   388\t   each return frame's activation base.\"\n   389\t  [frame]\n   390\t  {:yin.k/depth (count (:stack frame)),\n   391\t   :yin.k/bound (vec (sort-by str (keys (:env frame)))),\n   392\t   :yin.k/stack-bases (mapv :stack-base (:k frame))})\n   393\t\n   394\t\n   395\t(defn unsatisfied-names\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
